{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Issachar, a donkey.</b> Unfit for war, as they said (Avodah Zarah 17b): אִי סַפְרָא לָא סַיְפָא (a scholar does not bear a sword)." "<b>Bone — a donkey.</b> Possessing a strong bone, and in his strength <b>couches between the saddlebags.</b> When he camps, he lies down between the two loads placed for carrying on either side — in the manner of setting two pots on a hearth so that they do not move until the worker completes his intention with them. This is impossible for anything but a very strong donkey that can lie down with the loads on his back. And so too <b>Issachar</b> bears upon himself the yoke of Torah and the yoke of proper conduct and governance of states, as is fitting for a sage perfected in character traits and in intelligibles."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:27.346685766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}